# edge-server run artifacts. Everything below is produced by a camera session on the operator's
# machine and must never be committed: roster.json holds ArcFace face templates (biometric data,
# one row per named student), out/ holds the document dumps, and the two weights files are
# downloads that belong to the library cache, not to git.
edge-server/roster.json
edge-server/out/
edge-server/pending_upload.jsonl
edge-server/config.local.yaml
edge-server/*.pt
edge-server/*.task
edge-server/service_account.json
edge-server/*.key
# Any weight file, wherever it lands. ultralytics writes the model into the CURRENT folder, so running
# main.py from the repo root used to drop a second 5.4 MB yolo11n.pt there and leave it in git status
# as an untracked binary someone might add. No .pt is tracked in this repo, so this costs nothing.
# .onnx joins for the same reason: `yolo11n.pt.export(format='onnx')` writes it next to the .pt, and an
# 11 MB export sitting in git status is exactly the trap the line above was written for.
*.pt
*.onnx
# focuschange.db is written by database/database.py the first time the program runs, and every
# session adds rows to it. It is measured data about named children, not source, so it must never
# be added. No .db is tracked in this repo, so this costs nothing.
*.db
*.db-journal
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
